
========================================================================
P1  Universal constant-term identity
========================================================================
S=(1, 2, 3, 4), m=2: CT[P^m Pbar^m]=44=direct additive energy
S=(1, 2, 4, 8), m=3: CT[P^m Pbar^m]=286=direct additive energy
S=(0, 1, 3, 7), m=3: CT[P^m Pbar^m]=286=direct additive energy
Survivor: the diagonal CT identity is exact; its relation support is affine (augmentation zero).

========================================================================
P2  Finite AP-energy scout, with its actual scope
========================================================================
N=8, k=5, m=2: best=85; AP maximizers=4/56 rows
N=8, k=5, m=3: best=1751; AP maximizers=4/56 rows
N=8, k=5, m=4: best=38165; AP maximizers=4/56 rows
N=9, k=5, m=2: best=85; AP maximizers=6/126 rows
N=9, k=5, m=3: best=1751; AP maximizers=6/126 rows
N=9, k=5, m=4: best=38165; AP maximizers=6/126 rows
N=10, k=6, m=2: best=146; AP maximizers=5/210 rows
N=10, k=6, m=3: best=4332; AP maximizers=5/210 rows
N=10, k=6, m=4: best=135954; AP maximizers=5/210 rows
Scope: nine finite censuses, not an all-k or all-order AP theorem; THM-730 counts a+b=c instead.

========================================================================
P3  No-carry tensorization and the AP carry obstruction
========================================================================
no-carry scale 5: E2(S1+scale*S2)=836=E2(S1)E2(S2)
target AP at carry scale 3: E2([0..11])=1156!=836=19*44
Thus separated-digit factorization is conditional and removes the carry relations driving AP energy.

========================================================================
P4  The missing augmentation coordinate
========================================================================
m=2: unanchored energies A,B,C all equal 85
m=3: unanchored energies A,B,C all equal 1751
m=4: unanchored energies A,B,C all equal 38165
but exact LRC maxima are (Fraction(1, 6), Fraction(1, 4), Fraction(1, 2))
anchored E2 values=(146, 130, 106); Schur counts=(10, 6, 0)=CT[P^2 Pbar]
Repair: retain M_(r,s)=CT[P^r Pbar^s]; r-s is the augmentation sidecar.

========================================================================
P5  Exact volume ceiling
========================================================================
S=(1, 2, 3): M=1/4; top fiber=(Fraction(1, 4), Fraction(3, 4)); Haar measure=0; Euler components=2
Positive safe measure certifies a strict exit; Euler characteristic also detects isolated equality.

========================================================================
SUMMARY
========================================================================
Exact survivors: diagonal and mixed CT identities, the finite AP scout, conditional no-carry
tensorization, and the volume/Euler boundary distinction.  Refuted: diagonal energy as the full
LRC lattice, THM-730 as an E2 theorem, arbitrary rank reduction, and a GMC radial-kernel swap.
Live repair: the mixed (r,s) table or an observer at zero restores augmentation; no implication yet.
